<task id="107" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>ISS-009 (#974) option A — invert the read default: a grant with NO sprk_expiresdate confers NOTHING</title>
    <phase>FR-33 External grant expiry (register-driven, owner rule 2026-09-15)</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization-path .cs in Infrastructure/ExternalAccess — this changes what every external caller can reach, in the fail-CLOSED direction. Two definitions of "expired" (the OData predicate and its in-memory mirror) must move together or /grant reports an outcome the reader contradicts.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The mechanism is now fully decided (owner D-1) and the edit is two adjacent members plus the tests that pin their old semantics. No mechanism choice remains.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <effort-reason>Small diff, large blast radius: the change is a deliberate access REMOVAL, and the characterization tests that currently pin "null never expires" must be inverted with intent rather than deleted to make a build pass.</effort-reason>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>🔴 CHANGED 2026-09-21 by the D-1 rescope. This task no longer touches src/dataverse/** — it modifies Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalParticipationService.cs, the project's declared EXCLUSIVE zone. It was marked parallel-safe=true only while it was a Dataverse-plugin task. It must NOT run alongside 054/055/056/088 or anything else in that zone.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>097</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours + an operator COUNT before deploy</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Register ISS-009 / GitHub #974. 🔴 RESCOPED 2026-09-21 (task 115 follow-on) to the owner's D-1 decision of 2026-09-19 — see notes/owner-decision-brief-2026-09-18.md §D-1. The prior version of this file specified a Dataverse-side default (plugin or entity-scope business rule) and required the read filter to stay UNCHANGED; both were retired by that decision, and every binding element still asserted them.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>🔴 THE ORIGINAL PREMISE OF THIS TASK IS RETIRED. Do NOT write a Dataverse plugin, and do NOT add a Dataverse-side default. The owner ruled on 2026-09-19 (D-1): **"We do not use Dataverse plugins."** Plugins are off the table REPO-WIDE and no ADR-002 exception is being sought.

ISS-009 is instead closed from the READ side. Today `ExpiryPredicate` treats a null `sprk_expiresdate` as "never expires", so a grant row created outside the BFF — through a form, the Web API, a flow or an import, all reachable because users hold Create on `sprk_externalrecordaccess` — confers access forever. Invert that default: **a row with no expiry confers NOTHING.** Undated becomes fail-closed rather than fail-open.

The other two halves of D-1 are SEPARATE, ALREADY-AUTHORED tasks. Do not absorb them: **117** is option B (the scheduled reconciliation job that stamps undated rows, reusing `ExternalGrantLifecycle.DefaultExpiry` rather than a second literal 90), and **118** is option C (retire the Create-privilege proxy — code before config).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. BFF authorization internals: the external-access read filters and their in-memory mirror. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>A `sprk_externalrecordaccess` row with a null `sprk_expiresdate` confers NO access on any path: the OData read filter excludes it, and the in-memory write-path mirror agrees. Both definitions of "expired" move together and remain a single source of truth. A row WITH an expiry is unaffected in either direction, including on the expiry date itself. The operator COUNT of currently-undated rows is documented and stated as a pre-deploy gate, because this change REMOVES access from every such row.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Register ISS-009 (task 097 code review). Since 097 the BFF never writes a grant without `sprk_expiresdate` — but the column is optional in Dataverse and users hold Create on the table, so non-BFF writes can still omit it, and the read filter treats null as never-expiring.

🔴 **THE OWNER DECISION THAT RESCOPED THIS TASK** (2026-09-19, D-1; verbatim in notes/owner-decision-brief-2026-09-18.md): *"We do not use Dataverse plugins."* → A + B, and C is in scope, not deferred. Plugins are OFF the table repo-wide; no ADR-002 exception is sought. **Task 107 is RESCOPED off every Dataverse-side mechanism.** Option **A** is: invert the read default so a null `sprk_expiresdate` confers NOTHING — drop the `eq null` branch from `ExpiryPredicate`.

**GROUND TRUTH, verified at HEAD 2026-09-21** (do not inherit; re-check before editing):

1. `ExpiryPredicate` — `ExternalParticipationService.cs:99-100`:
   `=> $"(sprk_expiresdate eq null or sprk_expiresdate ge {today:yyyy-MM-dd})";`
   It is the ONE string definition. `grep "sprk_expiresdate eq null"` over `src/**/*.cs` returns exactly this line. Both grant filters consume it — the contact filter (`:62`) and `BuildOrganizationGrantFilter` (`:71`) — as does `ExternalDataService.cs:1031`. So there is ONE site to change, not six; earlier notes counting "six server-side sites" were counting CONSUMERS of this hoisted predicate.

2. 🔴 **`ConfersAccessOn` — `ExternalParticipationService.cs:124-125` — IS THE PART THE OLD POML NEVER MENTIONED, AND IT IS THE RISK.**
   `=> expiresDate is null || expiresDate.Value >= today;`
   It is the IN-MEMORY MIRROR of `ExpiryPredicate`, deliberately adjacent to it, and the only in-memory expiry test in the external-access WRITE path (task 106). Its own doc comment states why: *"Two independent definitions of 'expired' is precisely the drift that would let `/grant` report an outcome the reader contradicts."* **If you change the predicate and not the mirror, `/grant` will tell a caller a grant is live while the reader denies it.** `SetRecordShareExpiryEndpoint` was deliberately routed through this method so the single-definition claim is true by construction — keep it true. (`GrantExpiryReminderJob`'s days-until-expiry arithmetic is NOT a mirror; it answers a different question. Leave it.)

3. **Tests that PIN THE CURRENT (about to be retired) SEMANTICS.** These must be inverted with intent and a recorded reason — never deleted to make a build go green:
   - `GrantExpiryCharacterizationTests.ExpiryPredicate_TreatsAGrantWithNoExpiryAsNeverExpiring` (`:90`) — its NAME states the retired rule.
   - `GrantExpiryCharacterizationTests` `:224` — the `ConfersAccessOn` mirror assertion.
   - `GrantLifecycleCharacterizationTests` `:955` — *"(`ExpiryPredicate`'s `eq null` branch), so that row confers access too."*
   - `ExternalAccessQueryIntegrityGuardTests` (`:40`, `:85`) — the guard asserting the builders append `ExpiryPredicate`; it should still pass unchanged, and if it does not, understand why before touching it.
   A prior measurement (notes/task-007-grant-expiry.md:112) recorded that dropping the `eq null` branch made **1 of 11** tests fail. Expect MORE than one now — that count predates tasks 097/100/106. Report the real number.

4. **This is an access REMOVAL, and the blast radius is data-dependent.** D-1 says "blast radius zero today but COUNT before deploy". Zero-today is a claim about live data, not about code, and it was not re-measured this session. Every currently-undated active grant row loses access the moment this deploys. The count is the gate.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalParticipationService.cs — `ExpiryPredicate` (:99-100) AND `ConfersAccessOn` (:124-125); both, or neither</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/GrantExpiryCharacterizationTests.cs — the characterization tests that pin the retired semantics</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/GrantLifecycleCharacterizationTests.cs — `:955`'s `eq null` assertion</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/SpaarkeCore/entities/sprk_externalrecordaccess/entity-schema.md — its "Expiry enforcement — NOT IMPLEMENTED" note (~:220) is stale since tasks 007 / 097 / 100</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/guides/EXTERNAL-ACCESS-ADMIN-SETUP.md — the pre-deploy COUNT command and what it means</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs — the BFF's own default (task 097)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/owner-decision-brief-2026-09-18.md §D-1 — the ruling this task now implements</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-007-grant-expiry.md — why the `eq null` branch was added in the first place; read it before removing it</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="097" status="completed">The BFF-side default — after it, the BFF itself never writes an undated grant, which is what makes inverting the read default safe for BFF-written rows.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner D-1 2026-09-19">🔴 BINDING, DO NOT RE-LITIGATE. "We do not use Dataverse plugins." Scope: the whole task. No plugin, no entity-scope business rule, no Dataverse-side default, no ADR-002 exception request. If the answer seems to require one, that is an escalation, not a decision.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the two definitions. `ExpiryPredicate` and `ConfersAccessOn` MUST change in the same commit and MUST remain semantically identical. A test pins their agreement; if no such test exists after this task, the task is not done.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail closed. The whole point of this change is that the undated case moves from fail-OPEN to fail-CLOSED. Do not add a compensating fallback that restores the old behaviour for "safety" — that would reinstate exactly what is being removed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="review-2026-08-24">Scope: verification. Perturbation is mandatory; pair positives with negatives. A test that still passes when the `eq null` branch is restored is not pinning this change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests stay at KEEP paths (tests/integration/auth/**). Characterization tests are INVERTED with a recorded reason, never deleted to make the build pass. Rename any test whose NAME asserts the retired rule.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-04">Scope: deployment. Code + docs only; the live operator COUNT and the deploy itself are operator steps — document them, do not execute them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">BFF-touching: state the placement decision citing .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md; report publish size (ceiling 60 MB). This is an in-place edit of an existing service, so expect ~0.00 MB — but measure against a FRESH master build, never the recorded baseline.</constraint>
  </constraints>

